      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><style>
  :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; background: transparent; }
  body {
    font: 13.5px/1.55 -apple-system, "SF Pro Text", system-ui, sans-serif;
    color: #23222b; padding: 4px 2px 10px;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  .badge {
    display: inline-block; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .5px;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: #fff; padding: 3px 9px; border-radius: 999px;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #7c6cff, #4f8bff);
  }
  h1.title {
    font-size: 19px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -.2px;
    margin: 11px 0 2px; color: #1b1a22;
  }
  ul.feats { list-style: none; margin: 14px 0 0; padding: 0; }
  ul.feats li {
    position: relative; padding: 9px 4px 9px 22px; margin: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(120,120,140,.14);
  }
  ul.feats li:first-child { border-top: 0; }
  ul.feats li::before {
    content: ""; position: absolute; left: 4px; top: 15px;
    width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #7c6cff, #4f8bff);
  }
  ul.feats li strong { color: #4f46e5; font-weight: 700; }
  p { margin: 8px 0; }
  code {
    font: 12px "SF Mono", ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace;
    background: rgba(120,120,140,.14); padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 5px;
  }
  a { color: #4f8bff; text-decoration: none; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    body { color: #d9d8e2; }
    h1.title { color: #f2f1f7; }
    ul.feats li { border-top-color: rgba(255,255,255,.09); }
    ul.feats li strong { color: #a99dff; }
    code { background: rgba(255,255,255,.10); }
  }
</style></head><body><span class="badge">Version 1.6.0</span><h1 class="title">A real dpm command line</h1><ul class="feats">
<li><strong>One-click CLI install</strong> — Settings → Command line now puts <code>dpm</code> on your PATH with a single button, and tells you if it points at an old copy.</li>
<li><strong>Command line, redesigned</strong> — Every command has its own tab with an options table, required and default tags, copyable examples and colour-coded exit codes.</li>
<li><strong>New CLI commands</strong> — <code>dpm devices</code> lists connected devices and simulators, <code>dpm apps</code> lists installed packages, and <code>dpm help &lt;command&gt;</code> explains any command. Typos get a &quot;did you mean&quot; instead of opening the app.</li>
<li><strong>Smarter CI gates</strong> — <code>dpm record</code> adds a <code>--max-cpu</code> budget, writes a min/avg/max summary and a pass/fail gate into the JSON, shows live progress, and fails clearly when the app isn&#x27;t running.</li>
<li><strong>A refined Liquid Glass icon</strong> — The app icon is now a layered Icon Composer icon, so it gets the glass look on macOS 26 and 27.</li>
<li><strong>macOS 27 fixes</strong> — Built and tested against the macOS 27 SDK, with Swift 6 concurrency and deprecated file-dialog fixes.</li>
</ul></body></html>]]></description>
